Story: Taking off with the TX15
  As a pilot with a radio
  I want to arm the VTOL, pick a hover mode and lift off with the throttle stick
  So that I can fly the plane the way I fly it in the field

  This tutorial starts with the station and ends with a landing. The station opens three
  windows: the console, the sensor feed and the sim. The plane is on the ground at the pilot
  box. You arm the plane with SE and pick QLOITER with button 2. Push the
  throttle stick up, and the plane climbs straight up. Put the stick in the middle, and the
  plane keeps its height. Pull the stick down, and the plane lands.

  Scenario: Arm, pick QLOITER, lift off and land
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 5 m
    When the throttle stick is middle
    Then the flight is hovering
    When the throttle stick is low
    Then the plane is on the ground

Story: Flying a VTOL with self-levelling
  As a pilot learning to fly a VTOL
  I want the plane to level itself when I let go of the sticks
  So that I can fly it forward, bring it back to a hover and land it softly while I learn

  This tutorial follows [[Taking off with the TX15]] and uses the same radio. You lift off
  in QLOITER. Then you press button 3 for FBWA, and the plane flies forward on its wing. In
  FBWA the plane levels itself, so you bank it with the aileron stick and then let go. At the
  end you press button 2 to hover again, and you press button 6. The plane flies home and lands softly.

  Scenario: Lift off, fly forward in FBWA, hover again and land softly
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    When the pilot switches to forward flight
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    When the aileron stick is right
    Then the VTOL's wings are banked
    When the aileron stick is centred
    Then the VTOL's wings are level
    When the pilot switches back to a hover
    Then the flight is hovering
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the autopilot mode is QRTL
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the last landing is soft

Story: Trying the buttons of the radio
  As a pilot with a radio
  I want to try the flight modes on the six buttons
  So that I know what each mode does before I fly a real flight

  This tutorial uses the same radio as [[Taking off with the TX15]]. You lift off in QLOITER, and
  then you try the other modes in the air. Button 1 is QHOVER, and the plane drifts with the wind.
  Button 4 is CRUISE, and the plane flies forward on its wing. Button 6
  is QRTL, and the plane flies home and lands softly. [[Flying a VTOL with self-levelling]] shows
  button 3, FBWA.

  Scenario: Lift off, try QHOVER and CRUISE, then fly home
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    When the pilot switches to QHOVER
    Then the autopilot mode is QHOVER
    And the flight is hovering
    When the pilot switches to cruise
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is CRUISE
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the autopilot mode is QRTL
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the last landing is soft

